+# GPU Node Autoscaling Notes
+
+- Use your cloud provider's cluster autoscaler with GPU node-pool scaling (e.g., GKE/AKS/EKS autoscaling groups).
+- Pre-warm capacity for predictable demand if node provisioning latency (3-10 minutes) is unacceptable for interactive workloads.
+- Combine with job queueing and KEDA so that workloads are queued while new nodes provision.
+- Consider using node-pool taints and pod tolerations to isolate GPU workloads.
